<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank market report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank market report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds were heartened by news the European Commission expects Spain to make good on its pledge to reduce the budget deficit to three percent of GDP this year from 4.4 percent last year.</p>
<p>Reaction was muted as Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato had earlier said the EU would pass Spain and because the EU had not been expected to turn an extremely critical eye to its member countries.</p>
<p>&quot;The EU rarely says anything ugly about these matters,&quot; said Henrik Lumholdt, economist at Bank of America in Madrid.</p>
</text>
